+  `(2 + o_d(1)) log(d)/d`.  Equivalently, it typically contains about
+  `2 n log(d)/d` vertices from **each** side.
+- Theorem 9 proves that local algorithms reach only
+  `(1 + o_d(1)) log(d)/d` vertices per side.
